# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://rangka-os.github.io/rangka-os/schema/0.5/module.json
name: loyalty
version: 1.0.0
title: {id: Member dan poin, en: Loyalty}
summary:
  id: Member, poin, tier member dan saldo deposit pelanggan di kasir.
  en: Members, points, member tiers and customer deposits at the counter.
category: sales
icon: vip-crown-line
# Members of a shop (rangka-apps#102). A member (loyalty_account) is signed up at the counter or the desk with a name
# and a WhatsApp number (one member per number, per org); flow loyalty_account_on_create links or makes its customer
# and gives it the base tier. A tier (member_tier) sets how many points a rupiah earns, what a point is worth when
# redeemed, the share of a bill points may pay, the member discount and the points' expiry; a member's figures are
# copied from its tier, so a sale reads them in one hop (also on a device, rangka-os contract 0058 §10).
# At the counter (module pos, rangka-os contract 0069 checkout slot) the cashier picks the member, redeems points as a
# discount and pays part or all of the bill from the member's deposit. Flow loyalty_on_sale checks the balances again
# under the flow read lock of contract 0025 and writes the append-only ledgers (contract 0026): loyalty_entry
# (points) and deposit_entry (rupiah). A void gives both back.
# Books: points stay off the books in v1 (a redemption is a discount, the sale's revenue is already net); the
# dashboard shows what the open points are worth. A deposit is a customer advance (2-1400 Uang muka pelanggan): a
# top-up (deposit_topup) and a refund (deposit_refund) are journalled by the accounting module, PPN is due when the
# deposit is spent, on the sale, as on any receipt. No top-up bonus in v1.
requires: {rangka: '>=0.5', users: ^1.2, contacts: ^1.4}
optional: {outlets: ^1.5, pos: ^1.5, payments: ^1.7, accounting: ^1.4}
